---
import EnglishHeader from '../../components/EnglishHeader.astro';
import EnglishFooter from '../../components/EnglishFooter.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"/><meta name="description" content="How The Evolution of Bikes processes personal data from comments, story submissions and newsletter subscriptions."/><title>Privacy · The Evolution of Bikes</title><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin/><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=Libre+Caslon+Display&display=swap" rel="stylesheet"/><link rel="stylesheet" href={`${base}/styles/global.css`}/></head>
<body><EnglishHeader danishPath="/privatliv/"/><main><article class="privacy-page"><header class="privacy-hero"><p class="section-label">Privacy</p><h1>When you share<br/><em>with us</em></h1><p>Here you can see what information we store, why we store it and what rights you have.</p></header><div class="privacy-body">
<section><h2>Who is responsible?</h2><p>Henning Renita Yde, The Evolution of Bikes, is the data controller for information submitted through the form.</p><p><strong>Contact:</strong> <a href="mailto:hyde@hyde.dk">hyde@hyde.dk</a></p></section>
<section><h2>What do we store?</h2><p>We store the title, place, period and story or comment you write, as well as your name, email address, choice of credit, and any photographs and information about them that you submit. For comments, we also store the address of the story to which the contribution belongs. Limited technical information is stored to protect against misuse.</p></section>
<section><h2>Why, and on what legal basis?</h2><p>The information is used to receive, assess, research and edit stories and comments, contact you about missing details and prepare a possible publication. Processing is based on your consent. A submission is not published automatically, and your email address is never displayed on the website.</p></section>
<section><h2>Who processes the information?</h2><p>The material is available only to the editorial team and trusted data processors providing technical storage. The form's private database and images are stored with Supabase. The information is not sold or used for marketing.</p></section>
<section><h2>The newsletter</h2><p>When you subscribe to the newsletter, we store your email address and evidence of your consent. The information is used only to send news from The Evolution of Bikes. Subscriptions and mailings are handled by Brevo as a data processor, and you must confirm your subscription by email.</p><p>You may withdraw your consent at any time through the unsubscribe link in the newsletter. Mailings will then stop, and the information will be deleted or restricted to what is necessary to document the previous subscription.</p></section>
<section><h2>How long do we keep it?</h2><p>Submissions that are not taken further are deleted no later than 12 months after the editorial decision. If a story is published, the material and necessary documentation of permissions may be retained for as long as the story remains published, or as long as needed to document the basis for publication.</p></section>
<section><h2>Your rights</h2><p>You may withdraw your consent and request access, correction, deletion, restriction or a copy of your information. You may also object to the processing. Write to <a href="mailto:hyde@hyde.dk">hyde@hyde.dk</a>. Withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of processing already carried out.</p><p>You may lodge a complaint with the <a href="https://www.datatilsynet.dk/english" rel="external">Danish Data Protection Agency</a>. No automated decisions or profiling take place.</p></section>
</div><p class="privacy-updated">Last updated 8 September 2026.</p><a class="privacy-back" href={`${base}/en/`}>Back to the home page</a></article></main><EnglishFooter/></body></html>
